# SSOP live-fire drill rule — controlled test beacon detection
# Matches DNS queries to the drill beacon domain. Uses dns.queries.rrname
# which matches query names in BOTH request and response messages (robust
# against resolver behavior). sid space: 9900000+ reserved for SSOP custom.
alert dns any any -> any any (msg:"SSOP DRILL: beacon domain DNS query"; dns.queries.rrname; content:"beacon-test.ssop.local"; nocase; sid:9900001; rev:1;)
# Threat-class variant: same beacon, ET-MALWARE-style description. Fires
# alongside 9900001; the analyst's threat-desc gate sees "ET MALWARE" and
# escalates (or lifts a tuned-FP override). Used to prove the evidence-gated
# tuning override on live data. NOTE: match content differs from 9900001
# (ssop.local vs beacon-test.ssop.local) so Suricata doesn't dedupe the
# identical rule — two same-match rules collapse to one; both must load.
alert dns any any -> any any (msg:"ET MALWARE SSOP Lab C2 Beacon beacon-test.ssop.local"; dns.queries.rrname; content:"ssop.local"; nocase; sid:9900002; rev:1;)
